--- !u!114 &1243112178305860953
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 3830629912306956029}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7b2938433f063553a6bf70a816112101, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  portraitImage: {fileID: 863217690359043194}
  descriptionText: {fileID: 7728976434025209689}
  prevButton: {fileID: 6567905283350454888}
  nextButton: {fileID: 2932773370965725720}
  scrollRect: {fileID: 4167840652416244262}
  titleFormat: <size=38><color=#FED66D>{0}</color></size>
  startIndex: 0
  entries:
  - title: ARCHER
    portrait: {fileID: -7615759149648210162, guid: 4a0f7e751266c8b49b98b8f30037928e, type: 3}
    description: 'Ranged attacker - shoots arrows over your front line.


      <color=#FED66D>Cost:</color>
      40 gold

      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color> 50

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color>
      15

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color> 13 (longest after the Catapult)

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color>
      3


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      Stops as soon
      as an enemy is inside its range and keeps shooting arrows at it. Each arrow
      damages the first enemy it touches.

      Allied melee units are allowed to
      walk through the Archer and the Archer steps back behind them, so it can keep
      firing from a safe distance.


      <size=30><color=#6DFE6E>GOOD AGAINST:</color></size>
      large groups of melee units that it can outrange.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>WEAK
      AGAINST:</color></size> anything that reaches it - 50 health does not last
      long.'
  - title: BASESLIME
    portrait: {fileID: -1182821291677670348, guid: 47e7edc1ab577f5409a147dd1765f465, type: 3}
    description: 'Basic melee fighter - the cheapest unit in the game.


      <color=#FED66D>Cost:</color>
      10 gold

      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color> 45

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color>
      10

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color> 3

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color>
      3


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      Hops forward
      and attacks the first enemy it meets, hitting until one of them dies. Allied
      melee units queue up behind it instead of pushing through it, so a BaseSlime
      in front also shields the units behind.


      <size=30><color=#6DFE6E>GOOD
      AGAINST:</color></size> filling the front line and soaking up damage on a small
      budget.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>WEAK AGAINST:</color></size> tougher
      enemies - 10 damage per hit is the lowest in the game, so it needs friends
      to finish the job.'
  - title: CATAPULT
    portrait: {fileID: 2668676513185622867, guid: 29222b4cb32810a47bacabd7914dc778, type: 3}
    description: 'Siege vehicle - the longest range in the game.


      <color=#FED66D>Cost:</color>
      60 gold

      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color> 70

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color>
      30

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color> 20

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color>
      2.5


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      Rolls forward
      instead of hopping, stops when an enemy is within 20 units and lobs a heavy
      stone at it. Nothing else can hit that far, so it reaches enemy Slingers and
      Archers long before they can answer.

      Allied melee units are allowed
      to walk through the Catapult and it parks behind them.


      <size=30><color=#6DFE6E>GOOD
      AGAINST:</color></size> ranged units, and chipping the enemy King from far
      away.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>WEAK AGAINST:</color></size> fast pushes
      - 2.5 speed makes it arrive late, and 70 health does not last long on its own.'
  - title: KINGBLUE
    portrait: {fileID: -1984228819797356573, guid: c20cf6042b7c79146bc5c004506836ed, type: 3}
    description: 'Your castle - the base you have to protect.


      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color>
      500

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color> 0

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color>
      none, it cannot attack

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color> 0, it never moves


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      The
      King is not a fighter: it never moves, never attacks, and it is the target
      every enemy unit marches towards.

      It is also your income. Every <color=#FED66D>2-4
      seconds</color> it drops <color=#FED66D>5 gold</color>, but it stops producing
      gold while it is under attack, so an enemy at your gate also cuts off your
      money. Each castle upgrade adds <color=#FED66D>+25%</color> to that income.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>If
      your King is destroyed you lose the match.</color></size>'
  - title: SLINGER
    portrait: {fileID: -584294941907073061, guid: 54312b8762709d74aa2bb75f8b80973d, type: 3}
    description: 'Cheap ranged attacker - slings small stones.


      <color=#FED66D>Cost:</color>
      20 gold

      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color> 30

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color>
      9

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color> 10

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color>
      3


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      Stops when an
      enemy is within 10 units and throws stones at it until one of them dies. It
      is the cheapest way to add damage from behind your front line.

      Allied
      melee units are allowed to walk through it and it stays behind the melee line.


      <size=30><color=#6DFE6E>GOOD
      AGAINST:</color></size> adding cheap damage to a push.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>WEAK
      AGAINST:</color></size> anything that reaches it - at 30 health a SpearMan
      needs only two hits.'
  - title: SPEARMAN
    portrait: {fileID: -3711943079083384488, guid: aea32d10050c9004da2826616b5f0343, type: 3}
    description: 'Tanky melee fighter with the longest melee reach.


      <color=#FED66D>Cost:</color>
      50 gold

      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color> 100

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color>
      28

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color> 6.4

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color>
      3


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      Stabs the first
      enemy in range. With 6.4 units of reach it can hit over the ally standing in
      front of it, and with 100 health it is the toughest fighter you can send.


      <size=30><color=#6DFE6E>GOOD
      AGAINST:</color></size> holding the front line and trading hits with anything
      red.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>WEAK AGAINST:</color></size> ranged units
      that stay outside its reach.'
  - title: SWORD
    portrait: {fileID: -4291930625038005619, guid: 52faec4ccc34ef64b9d082f505adb24e, type: 3}
    description: 'Fast melee fighter - the quickest of your ground units.


      <color=#FED66D>Cost:</color>
      30 gold

      <color=#FED66D>Health:</color> 65

      <color=#FED66D>Damage:</color>
      16

      <color=#FED66D>Range:</color> 3.1

      <color=#FED66D>Speed:</color>
      3.2


      <size=30><color=#FED66D>EFFECT</color></size>

      Runs at the
      enemy faster than any other unit and hits the first one in range. Its reach
      is as short as a BaseSlime''s, so it has to be right next to its target, but
      it deals 60% more damage and has 20 more health.


      <size=30><color=#6DFE6E>GOOD
      AGAINST:</color></size> escorting ranged units and cutting down BaseSlime.

      <size=30><color=#FF7B6B>WEAK
      AGAINST:</color></size> a SpearMan front line - it cannot reach past a screen
      of enemies.'
